      "created_at": "2026-08-10T22:55:28Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-10T22:55:28Z",
      "body": "Closing without merge. Build-testing against the FULL workspace test compile (which my earlier gauntlet skipped) shows all three modules this PR gated — lie_jordan, endomorphism, and packed_kernels — are referenced by the root BDD validation suite (tests/bdd.rs): lie_jordan (universal_product_u8, LieJordanSplit + a source-embed test), endomorphism (EndomorphismAlgebra), and packed_kernels (PackedFrontier/PackedShortlist/StepOutput). Gating them default-off breaks the default `cargo test --test bdd` build.\n\nPer the corrected preserve-and-gate rule (only modules with zero default-build reference — code or tests — are gated; modules with live default-suite coverage stay registered-but-compiled, like the CLI-reachable bott_fock/cd_space), none of these three are gatable. Their `open` ledger claims (lie-jordan-dormant, endomorphism-dormant, packed-routing-dormant) remain accurate — dormant in the serving path, with BDD validation harnesses — and are unchanged on main. Nothing to ship here. Refs #515.",
